---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const task = "The paid-revenue total is wrong. Reproduce it with the existing tests. Find the cause and propose the smallest fix.\n\nExpected paid revenue: $1,430.00. Exclude refunded, cancelled and pending invoices. Keep arithmetic in integer cents.\n\nShow the failing case before changing code. Explain the change, run the tests, and show the actual app result. Keep the change within this task.";
const skill = "---\nname: reproduce-and-fix\ndescription: Reproduce a reported bug, identify its cause, and verify a small fix.\n---\n\n1. Read the report and relevant project instructions.\n2. Reproduce the behavior with existing tests or a concrete input.\n3. Explain the cause using the code and observed output.\n4. Make the smallest change that solves the reported behavior.\n5. Run relevant checks and inspect the actual result.\n6. Report the change, evidence, and any remaining uncertainty.\n";
const review = "Review the patch in [PROJECT PATH], using [BASE REF OR COMMIT RANGE] as the comparison. The reported bug is [EXPECTED VS ACTUAL BEHAVIOR].\n\nCheck whether the patch fixes the bug, whether its scope is justified, and whether verification covers the changed behavior. Cite concrete problems with file locations. If you find no material issue, say so and state what you checked. Do not change files.";
const referenceFix = "export function paidRevenue(invoices) {\n  return invoices.filter(invoice => invoice.status === 'paid')\n    .reduce((total, invoice) => total + invoice.amountCents, 0);\n}\n";
---
<BaseLayout title="The small AI engineering setup — Prompt &amp; Done">
<main>
<nav><a href="/">Prompt &amp; Done</a><span>HARNESS checklist</span></nav>
<header><h1><span>Start small.</span><span>Finish the work.</span></h1><p class="intro">One harness, a coding agent, a few useful skills, and connections to the systems your job needs. Here's the starter setup from the reel.</p><a class="download" href="/downloads/harness-starter.zip" download>Download the bug demo + skill</a><p class="meta">Synthetic sample data · Node.js 20+ · Python 3 for the browser demo</p><ol class="checklist" aria-label="Starter setup checklist"><li><a href="#start">Install T3 Code and connect one coding agent.</a></li><li><a href="#try">Open a project and give it a clear task.</a></li><li><a href="#skills">Add a skill for a workflow you repeat.</a></li><li><a href="#mcp">Connect an approved MCP when the task needs company data.</a></li><li><a href="#delegate">Delegate a distinct job when it helps.</a></li><li><a href="#try">Check the reasoning, tests and actual result.</a></li></ol></header>
<section aria-labelledby="start"><h2 id="start">Choose your harness and agent</h2><ol><li>Install <a href="https://t3.codes">T3 Code</a> from the official site.</li><li>Choose an available coding agent and authenticate with its provider.</li><li>Open your project. Give the agent a concrete outcome and relevant constraints.</li></ol><p>T3 Code brings agents into one workspace. Your chosen agent does the coding; its subscription or API charges still apply.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="try"><h2 id="try">Try the exact bug from the reel</h2><p>Unzip the download. In its folder, run <code>node --test revenue.test.mjs</code>. The starting code wrongly counts a refunded invoice: <strong>$1,830.00</strong> instead of <strong>$1,430.00</strong>.</p><p>For the app view, run <code>python3 -m http.server 8000</code> and open <code>http://localhost:8000</code>. Keep that server running while the agent fixes the code.</p><div class="prompt"><h3>A clear task</h3><pre>{task}</pre><button type="button" data-copy="task">Copy task prompt</button><p class="copy-status" aria-live="polite"></p></div><p>After the fix, run the four tests and refresh the browser. Read the diff yourself. Compare with the reference below after you have tried the task.</p><details><summary>Reveal the reference fix after trying the task</summary><pre>{referenceFix}</pre></details></section>
<section aria-labelledby="skills"><h2 id="skills">Keep skills for repeat work</h2><p>A skill packages a workflow you use repeatedly. Start with the one in the download; add more when the work calls for them.</p><p>For Codex, save this as <code>.agents/skills/reproduce-and-fix/SKILL.md</code> in your project. Other agents may use different locations.</p><details><summary>View the focused skill</summary><pre>{skill}</pre><button type="button" data-copy="skill">Copy skill template</button><p class="copy-status" aria-live="polite"></p></details></section>
<section aria-labelledby="mcp"><h2 id="mcp">Connect the data you actually need</h2><p>Add an MCP server when a task needs a company system. A good starting tool might retrieve a specific invoice, issue or document.</p><ul><li>Use approved read-only access first.</li><li>Give each tool a specific purpose, small input schema and compact result.</li><li>Keep credentials in supported secret or environment configuration.</li><li>Set it up through your chosen agent's supported MCP settings.</li></ul><p>The reel describes a personal company setup. This download uses sample data and includes no private company MCP configuration.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="delegate"><h2 id="delegate">Give another agent a distinct job</h2><p>T3 has <a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/blob/main/apps/server/src/mcp/toolkits/orchestrator/tools.ts">built-in orchestration tools</a>. Use it for a bounded investigation or independent patch review when that separate job is useful. Give it the files, constraints and expected return.</p><details><summary>View the independent review brief</summary><pre>{review}</pre><button type="button" data-copy="review">Copy review brief</button><p class="copy-status" aria-live="polite"></p></details><p>Additional agents can add latency and token use. Check their conclusions before you merge or ship.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="context"><h2 id="context">Keep loaded context relevant</h2><p>Installing a tool or skill doesn't necessarily load all of it. Definitions, instructions and returned data are what can occupy context. Prefer scoped results and on-demand discovery where your provider supports them.</p><p>Anthropic's roughly 55,000-token example came from five eagerly loaded MCP servers in a published 2025 setup. Chroma studied reliability as input length grew. Neither establishes a universal limit on plugin counts.</p><p>Start with the work. Add what helps you finish it.</p></section>
<footer><h2>Sources and setup docs</h2><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code">T3 Code source and docs</a></li><li><a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/build-skills">Codex skill structure</a></li><li><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/advanced-tool-use">Anthropic: advanced tool use</a></li><li><a href="https://www.trychroma.com/research/context-rot">Chroma: context rot</a></li></ul><p>Checked 11 October 2026 · Prompt &amp; Done</p></footer>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
<script define:vars={{task,skill,review}}>
const texts={task,skill,review};
document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',async()=>{const status=button.nextElementSibling;try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(texts[button.dataset.copy]);status.textContent='Copied. Paste it into your agent.';setTimeout(()=>{status.textContent=''},3500);}catch{status.textContent='Copy failed. Select the text above and copy it manually.'}}));
</script>
<style>
main{width:min(100% - 2.5rem,46rem);margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 0 3rem}nav{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--soft);margin:0 0 4rem}nav a{font-weight:900;text-decoration:none}h1{font-size:clamp(2.9rem,11vw,5rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:0;color:var(--ink);font-weight:900;text-wrap:balance}h1 span{display:block}h1 span:last-child{color:var(--accent)}.intro{font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.6;max-width:39rem;margin:1.5rem 0;color:var(--soft)}a{color:var(--accent);text-underline-offset:.2em}.download,button{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:48px;background:var(--accent);color:#191100;border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:.8rem 1.1rem;font-family:inherit;font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;cursor:pointer}.download:hover,button:hover{background:#ffd08a}.meta{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--soft);line-height:1.6}section{margin-top:3.5rem;padding-top:2rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}h2{font-size:1.7rem;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:0 0 1rem;font-weight:900;text-wrap:balance}h3{font-size:1rem;margin:0 0 1rem}p,li{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7;color:var(--soft);max-width:68ch}li{color:var(--ink)}.checklist a{color:var(--ink)}.checklist a:hover{color:var(--accent)}.checklist{margin:1.75rem 0 0;padding:1.5rem 1.5rem 1.5rem 2.5rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:#101011}li+li{margin-top:.55rem}ol,ul{padding-left:1.5rem}strong{color:var(--ink)}code{color:var(--ink);font-size:.86em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.prompt{margin:1.7rem 0}pre{font:400 .9rem/1.7 ui-monospace,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;margin:1rem 0 1.25rem;padding:1.25rem;background:#141415;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;color:var(--ink)}details{margin:1.25rem 0}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--accent);min-height:44px;line-height:1.5;padding:.6rem 0}details[open] summary{color:var(--ink)}.copy-status{min-height:1.7em;font-size:.85rem;margin:.5rem 0 0}footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:3.5rem;padding-top:2rem}footer h2{font-size:1.2rem}footer p{font-size:.85rem}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ffd08a;outline-offset:5px}::selection{background:#ffb454;color:#191100}@media(max-width:480px){h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,10.5vw,3.8rem)}nav{margin:0 0 3rem}nav span{font-size:.78rem}.download{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}section{margin-top:2.5rem}}
</style>
